%% Sequence 04e — Persist signed AI dispute callback
%% Evidence status: Partial. Callback verification and atomic persistence are implemented; advisory output depends on the configured external service.
%% Parent use case: UC 03b “Inspect AI advisory”; external service completion triggers this technical callback scenario.
%% Design-class trace: cls_03l_ai_dispute_callback_runtime_design defines the boundary, factory, command, cryptography, and unit-of-work responsibilities used by this scenario.
%% Scenario: the external advisory service completes one existing evaluation.
%% Scope: callback trust boundary and persistence. Human resolution is seq_04c.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant X as «external» Clawagent advisory API
    participant C as «boundary» AiDisputeCallbackController
    participant K as «control» ProcessAiDisputeCallbackCommand
    participant H as «outbound» HMAC verifier
    participant U as «outbound» AI dispute unit of work
    participant DB as «store» PostgreSQL

    X->>C: POST /api/public/ai-disputes/callback
    C->>K: execute(evaluation id, status, timestamp, signature, advice)
    activate K
    K->>H: Verify timestamp and HMAC
    H-->>K: Authentic or reject
    K->>U: run atomic callback persistence
    U->>DB: Load evaluation and source identity
    DB-->>U: Evaluation status and identifiers
    alt Valid queued/processing evaluation
        U->>DB: Store completed/failed advice payload
        U->>DB: Transition ai_reviewing source to human-review state
        DB-->>U: Persisted terminal advisory result
        U-->>K: Callback result
        K-->>C: id, disputeId, status
        C-->>X: 200 callback accepted
    else Signature, identifier, or terminal-state conflict
        U-->>K: Reject callback
        K-->>C: Authorization/validation/conflict error
        C-->>X: Safe error response
    end
    deactivate K
    Note over U,DB: Advisory result, human resolution is recorded in seq_04c.
